  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "edd843cb-cfaf-49a3-ad9b-e765db7c5e4b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We can see that there are missing values on gender and credit limit. Age min value is -10 and max value is 150 which both seem unrealistic. Total spend min value is negative which isn't possible either.\n",
    "\n",
    "Next lets check if there is any duplicate values on CustomerID"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "60af5ada-54ee-4fb2-9436-2498169a97a4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "duplicates=df_customers[\"CustomerID\"].duplicated().sum()\n",
    "print(duplicates)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0137d919-9a2d-437c-a119-620219d6c2e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "All customerID are unique so we are working with 10 000 customers. Next lets make a boolean mask to filter out unrealistic ages. Lets start with range of 0-100 and see what the min and max values are after that. We can add negative TotalSpent values to the mask too."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "93ce8c5d-c3ed-492a-8402-67c598abc164",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "age_mask=(df_customers[\"Age\"]>0) & (df_customers[\"Age\"]<100) & (df_customers[\"TotalSpent\"]>=0)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "db08c441-7354-4333-a29f-e8bfcb509f36",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
